$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 71-43-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure for the Synthesis of 4aa A magnetic stirring bar, 1a
(240.8 mg, 1.0 mmol), 2a (150.5 mg, 1.5 mmol), 3 (302.1 mg, 1.2 mmol),
PdCl2 (9.0 mg, 0.05 mmol), LiCl (8.9 mg, 0.2 mmol), Et3N (151.0 mg, 1.5
mmol), and C6H6 (10 mL) were placed in Pyrex vial under Ar. Then, t-BuNC
(23 µL, 0.2 mmol) was added. The solution was irradiated with Solarbox
(Xe, 1000 W/m2) with violently stirring for 16 h. The reaction mixture
filtered and concentrated in vacuo to give a residue, which was subjected
to silica gel column chromatography using hexane/EtOAc = 50/1 as eluent,
4aa (131.0 mg, 0.71 mmol, 71%). ethyl 3-cyclohexylpropanoate (4aa)2
Colorless oil (131.0 mg, 0.71 mmol, 71%). 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 4.10
(q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 2.30-2.26 (m, 2H), 1.70-1.58 (m, 5H), 1.53-1.48 (m,
2H), 1.26-1.05 (m, 7H), 0.91-0.80 (m, 2H); 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ
174.29, 60.24, 37.31, 33.04, 32.44, 32.04, 26.60, 26.30, 14.32.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, regioselective, optimized on ligand, tin-free Giese
