$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure C: 3-Tridecanone (3m). A
magnetic stirring bar, n Bu4NBH3CN (311.7 mg, 1.5 mmol), 1a (118.6 mg,
0.49 mmol), 2f (127.1 mg, 1.5 mmol), and methanol (1.0 mL) were placed in
a Pyrex 10 mL round-bottomed flask and the mixture was irradiated by
Xenon arc lamp (500 W) with stirring for 6 h under argon. The solvent was
removed under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel (hexane/Et2O = 20/1) to give 3m.
5-Adamantyl-3-pentanone(3o) Pale yellow oil, yield 55 %. Pale vyellow
oil, (Rf = 0.18, hexane/ Et2O = 15/1); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 1.04 (t,
J = 7.4 Hz, 3H), 1.30-1.37 (m, 2H), 1.41-1.48 (m, 6H), 1.57-1.64 (m, 3H),
1.66-1.74 (m, 3H), 1.90-1.97 (m, 3H), 2.31-2.37 (m, 2H), 2.42 (q, J = 7.3
Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ 7.95, 28.61, 31.80, 35.81, 36.03,
37.08, 37.88, 42.17, 212.55; IR (neat) 1715 cm-1; MS (EI) m/z (rel
intensity) 220 (M+, 3), 202 (28), 191 (67), 173 (37), 135 (100), 107
(21), 93 (39), 91 (30), 79 (48), 67 (25), 57 (41); HRMS calcd for
C15H24O1 (M+) 220.1827, found 220.1830.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, regioselective, Tin-Free Giese Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
